1, Sass (SCSS) Global Installation & Direct Usage Guide

This guide outlines the steps to install the Sass compiler globally and execute
direct commands without relying on local project configurations (npm scripts).

1. Global Installation (One-Time Setup)

---

Install Dart Sass globally so the 'sass' command can be run from any directory.
NOTE: This step may require 'sudo' permissions on macOS/Linux.

Install the Sass compiler globally:
npm install -g sass

Verify installation:
sass --version

2. Directory Structure Setup

---

Before running the commands, ensure your project directory has the necessary folders and an input file.

Example structure (from your current working directory):

project/ (Current Directory)
|-- source/
| |-- stylesheets/
| | |-- index.scss (Sass source code INPUT - Create this file)
|-- build/
| |-- stylesheets/
| | |-- index.css (Compiled CSS OUTPUT)

3. Direct Sass Commands

---

These commands are run directly in the terminal, targeting the specific input and output files.

A. Manual Compilation (Single Run)
Use this to compile the file once and exit.

sass source/stylesheets/index.scss build/stylesheets/index.css

B. Development Mode (Continuous Watch) - RECOMMENDED
Use the --watch flag to automatically compile CSS every time you save changes to the input file.

sass --watch source/stylesheets/index.scss build/stylesheets/index.css

C. Production Build (Minified Output)
Creates a compressed version for deployment. This runs once and exits.

sass source/stylesheets/index.scss build/stylesheets/index.min.css --style=compressed

4. HTML Integration

---

Link the compiled CSS output file (e.g., index.css) in your HTML document.

<link rel="stylesheet" href="build/stylesheets/index.css" />

## Notes

- Since this is a global installation, you MUST use the full 'sass' command and file paths.
- The 'build/stylesheets' directory is generated output and should not be modified manually.
- SCSS features (variables, nesting, mixins) are fully supported.
